-- | The message `RDX1001` carries — doc 03 §12.7, plan 38.
-- |
-- | §12.7's substance is in the second half: the warning names **the ergonomic
-- | path**, and that is the only thing this lint has over
-- | `clippy::unwrap_used`. Plan 38 §2 is unusually frank about it — clippy can
-- | detect the same call; what it cannot do is say `??` and `catch`, or point
-- | at the `.sdx`.
-- |
-- | So the wording is the feature, which is why it lives in a named constant
-- | rather than inline at the construction site.
export(crate) const UNWRAP_MESSAGE : &str = "`unwrap` and `expect` panic — the ergonomic path is `?`, `??` or `catch` (doc 03 §12.7)"
